<!-- SPECIAL CASES -->
<div class="section-label">Troubleshooting</div>
<div class="section-title">Special Cases</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ The warranty has already expired</h3>
<p>Signia <strong>cannot extend</strong> an expired warranty. The hearing aid has to be repaired first.</p>
<ol>
<li>Don't order. Move the card to <strong>Needs Review</strong> and add a note with the expiration date shown in Signia.</li>
<li>Message Rhett. The customer will either get a refund, or switch to the <strong>Signia Hearing Aid Repair</strong> (same price). Once the repair is done, their aid is back under a 6-month warranty, and they can buy the extension then.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ I moved the card to Coverage Active before entering the date</h3>
<p>The customer already got a message with a blank or wrong date. Moving the card back and forward again <strong>will not resend it</strong>.</p>
<ol>
<li>Enter the correct <strong>Warranty End Date</strong> on the contact and save.</li>
<li>Open the contact's <span class="click">Conversations</span> and send this SMS by hand:</li>
</ol>
<div class="sms-box">
<div class="sms-label">Correction SMS (send manually)</div>
Hi [first name], correction from Hearing Benefit Services: your new Signia warranty expiration date is [date]. Sorry for any confusion! If you ever need a repair, call us at 808-435-7002.
</div>
<ol start="3">
<li>Add a note on the contact: "Sent corrected warranty end date [date]."</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>❗ The serial number isn't found in Signia, or doesn't match the model</h3>
<ol>
<li>Don't order. Leave the card in <strong>Registered - Ready to Order</strong>.</li>
<li>Call or text the customer to double-check the serial number (common mix-ups: 0/O, 1/I, 5/S, 8/B).</li>
<li>Update the <strong>Serial Number for Left / Right</strong> fields on the contact with the corrected number, then continue with the warranty check and order.</li>
<li>If it still can't be found, add a note and message Rhett.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>📞 The customer calls asking about their status</h3>
<p>Open their card in <strong>Opportunities → Signia Warranty Extension Purchase</strong>. The stage tells you exactly where they are:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="info-table">
<thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What to Tell Them</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Purchased - Awaiting Registration</td><td>"We still need your serial numbers." Help them submit the form.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Registered - Ready to Order</td><td>"We have your info and are confirming your warranty and placing the order with Signia now."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ordered with Signia</td><td>"It's been ordered. We'll text and email your new expiration date as soon as Signia confirms it."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Coverage Active</td><td>"You're covered!" Read them the <strong>Warranty End Date</strong> on their contact.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Needs Review</td><td>"We're looking into your registration and will contact you shortly." Check the notes and message Rhett if unsure.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>🔧 The customer calls for a repair (damaged hearing aid)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open their contact and confirm they have the tag <code>warranty-ext-active</code>.</li>
<li>Check that today is <strong>before</strong> their <strong>Warranty End Date</strong>.</li>
<li>If covered: process the repair through Signia as a warranty repair. <strong>No charge to the customer.</strong> Add a note on the contact.</li>
<li>If not covered (no tag, or the date has passed): offer the <strong>Signia Hearing Aid Repair</strong> product ($299, or $250 with code <code>JDSKXDH</code>).</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>🔍 The customer calls about a LOST hearing aid</h3>
<ol>
<li>Open their contact and confirm they have the tag <code>warranty-ext-active</code>, and that today is <strong>before</strong> their <strong>Warranty End Date</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>If covered:</strong> the replacement fee is <span class="highlight">$299 per lost hearing aid</span>. Collect payment (message Rhett for the payment link or invoice), then order the loss replacement in the Signia portal using the lost aid's serial number. Add a note with the Signia order number.</li>
<li><strong>If NOT covered:</strong> loss isn't covered once the warranty has expired. The customer needs a new hearing aid at standard pricing. Offer to book a consultation.</li>
</ol>
<div class="alert alert-info" style="margin-bottom:0;">
<strong>Note:</strong> The $299 fee is pending final confirmation from Andrea. Signia charges HBS $212 per aid for in-warranty loss &amp; damage replacement, with free shipping.
</div>
